   "text": "I read the structure in pieces and joined them into one SMILES, then checked the ring closures and assigned each stereocentre from the CIP priorities.\n\n**Fragments read from the image**\n- **Pyridine:** a 2-(1-methoxyethyl)pyridine, attached through its C3 to the indole C2. The methoxy-bearing carbon is (S).\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, with C3 carrying CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O)\u2013, which links to the piperazic acid. C5 is bonded to the tetrahydropyridine.\n- **Tetrahydropyridine:** N1CCC=C(C1)\u2013, with the ring carbon at the double bond attached to indole C5. The N carries a CH2 that leads to the chain below.\n- **Piperazic acid:** a six-membered ring N(acyl)\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013CH(C(=O)O\u2013)\u2013NH. The ester-bearing carbon is (S).\n- **Central chain:** N\u2013CH2\u2013CH(NH\u2013)\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(piperazic), with the CH as (S). The NH is acylated by an (S)-N-methylvaline whose N is a urea nitrogen.\n- **Urea end:** the urea carbonyl is bonded to a piperidine nitrogen. That piperidine is spiro-fused to an oxazolidine, O\u2013CH2\u2013N(acryloyl)\u2013CH(CH3), with the methyl-bearing CH as (S).\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nFor each centre I took the neighbour order as written in the SMILES, ranked the substituents by CIP priority and picked the tag that gives S. That gives `[C@H]` for the methoxy carbon, `[C@@H]` for the piperazic carbon, and `[C@H]` for the central CH, the valine \u03b1-carbon and the spiro-adjacent methyl CH.\n\nSMILES: CCn1c(-c2cccnc2[C@H](C)OC)c(CC(C)(C)COC(=O)[C@@H]2CCCN(N2)C(=O)[C@H](CN2CCC=C(C2)5)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)N(C)C(=O)N2CCC6(CC2)OCN(C(=O)C=C)[C@H]6C)c2cc5ccc12"
